& [SerdeAudit] is exact
  + PrepareRequest PreparedRunRequest VerifyRequest ProcedureToolResponse and all reachable public structures use actual serde Deserialize or Serialize forms
  + public object forms deny unknown fields unless the subject is an intentional map or set projection
  + SemanticId uses a custom deserializer enforcing nonempty maximum-512-byte ASCII alphanumeric underscore hyphen period colon slash identity
  + serde_json 1.0.151 is locked and retains its default recursive container limit
  + decoding bytes directly to a typed form preserves type and custom-deserializer behavior but does not expose a general proof that duplicate map keys were absent
  + decoding first to serde_json Value loses duplicate-key evidence and therefore cannot be the ingress authority

& [SchemaAudit] is exact
  + canonical dialect is https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema
  + all references in the five documents are local fragments and every target exists in the same document
  + objects are closed structurally except intended map projections
  + SemanticId min max and pattern appear in schema and are eligible for schema-serde agreement proof
  + root documents are syntax contracts only and contain no custom execution keywords
  + canonical artifacts are already verified before I03 and must be consumed read-only by expected path length digest id and dialect

& [SemanticEnforcementAudit] finds multiple non-syntactic families
  + recursive type and value depth plus value resource accounting remain RMS-R01 through RMS-R05
  + schema acceptance never grants authority under RMS-R06
  + prepare_response rejects pass_index equal to u64 maximum before later-pass increment
  + run_authorship_lane validates source digest provenance authority separation normalized forms receipts compilation verification fake admission catalogue coordination token passes stable session and replay
  + validate_schema requires the exact reconstructed provider-neutral profile and digest
  + validate_tool_call binds schema identity argument digest executable operation participant identity admitted invocation and lane evidence replay
  + verify_fake_controller_outcome binds zero provider and effect counters transcript digest event order completed-versus-refused shape result digest explicit context and exact replay
  + these are residual rules to catalogue rather than schema keywords to invent

& [DuplicateKeyAudit] resolves a false equivalence assumption
  + JSON Schema validates a parsed instance and cannot observe duplicate member spellings already collapsed by a generic object representation
  + ordinary typed serde decoding is not selected as the proof of duplicate absence
  + I03 requires an independent bounded recursive byte visitor that rejects duplicate keys before releasing a Value
  + duplicate-key corpus cases are byte-ingress cases; schema validation is not applicable after ingress refusal and serde behavior is recorded without being treated as the governing outcome

& [ValidatorCandidateAudit] is current as of 2026-08-05
  + jsonschema 0.49.2 was published 2026-07-27 and declares Rust 1.85 while workspace policy is Rust 1.96
  + official crate metadata exposes Draft 2020-12 APIs and meta-schema support
  + default features enable resolve-http resolve-file and tls-aws-lc-rs
  + default-features false disables built-in external resolution and is mandatory if selected
  + the crate is not present in Cargo.lock and no jsonschema-0.49.2 source or crate archive is currently cached locally
  + exact resolution transitive dependency lock offline retrieval audit and Windows Application Control execution are therefore activation blockers rather than formation blockers
  + technical references are https://docs.rs/crate/jsonschema/0.49.2 and https://github.com/Stranger6667/jsonschema

& [NumberBoundaryAudit] remains open for activation proof
  + public forms include u64 values and I02 schemas carry exact integer ceilings where generated
  + serde_json Value and validator numeric representations must be tested below at and above u64 maximum before agreement is claimed
  + enabling an arbitrary-precision feature could unify serde_json features across the workspace and is not authorized by formation
  + no numeric representation choice is silently inferred

& [ResourceAudit] inherits finite ceilings
